1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Modular Library

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Modular Library is a resource library that helps you quickly use and combine clothing items.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Right-click on the title on the left side of the page and click on the Modular Library.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
You can see that the Modular Library has been opened.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
If you are new here, you can see that there are three folders for children, men, and women.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Double-click to enter the next folder.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Here are some basic clothing types.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
If you are new here, you can see that there are basic shoes, make-up, shirt, jacket, polo shirt.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Double-click again to open Basic Sheets.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
After entering the specific style, you can see that the clothing has been divided into several large modules.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Each module has a rich array of items for you to switch.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Once you have selected it,

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
you need to click on the Modular Library.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Here are all the modules you need.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Press Shift A to hide the virtual model.

16
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Using the clothing created by the Modular Library,

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
the sewing relationship between the modules can be automatically identified.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Press B to display the sewing line.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
You will find that the sewing line has been automatically created.

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Use the button to simulate,

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:35,000
we got a piece of metal clothing quickly through the Modular Library.

22
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
You can quickly change the clothing here.

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
You can freely combine it to the clothing you want.

24
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
When you double-click to switch a particular item,

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,000
the item in the previous module will be replaced and disappeared.

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
When you double-click to switch a particular item,

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:01,000
So please save each piece of clothes in a timely manner to protect the safety of the file.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,000
To avoid the presence of more pieces of clothes in the scene, some panels will be replaced by hand.

29
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Continue to modify the clothing effect you want on the created basic clothing.

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Here we change the sleeves of the skirt into medium sleeves.

31
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:27,000
After modifying the satisfied effect, click on the plus sign in this column.

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Press Shift, select two sleeves, press Enter to confirm.

33
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Confirm the panel, then confirm the sewing relationship.

34
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
This self-defined part has been successfully stored.

35
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
You can quickly use it through the module library in the future.

36
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
You can create various self-defined parts and styles through the small plus signs in the upper right corner of each layer.

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Press the upper label to return to the last layer.

38
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Each layer can be created through the small plus sign to create a specific classification folder.

39
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:16,000
For example, now we have made a set of women's hanbok and want to add it to the module library.

40
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
So let's go to Woman first.

41
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Click on the small plus sign to create a new category named Hanbok.

42
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Enter the Hanbok category.

43
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Click on the small plus sign to add a style named Hanbok 1.

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Select Hanbok 1.

45
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Click on the small plus sign to add the required part type.

46
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:52,000
For example, this outfit is made up of front, back, sleeves, and collar.

47
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Then we need to add these four parts.

48
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Tips 2.

49
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Reglan refers to the clothes with a shoulder-in-shoulder style.

50
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The shoulder-in-shoulder style is more special due to the sewing relationship.

51
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
It is impossible to identify and create a sewing line with most clothes.

52
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
So the parts are listed separately.

53
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
If you don't have a shirt with a shoulder-in-shoulder style, don't choose Reglan.

54
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
After adding all the necessary parts,

55
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:29,000
click on the small star next to the top of the small plus sign to automatically model and draw a label.

56
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
You can see that each module is automatically identified.

57
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Check if there is a mistake in identification.

58
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Click on the small Families to add part effects and Confirm.

59
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Click on the small Sachein and type the part image.

60
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Click shift stupid and add paper with much 170 body parts and confirm by pressing the Enter key.

61
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Check if there is a mistake and add paper with much 170 body parts and confirm.

62
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:35,000
After confirming all, click on Add, and you can see that this Hanfu is stored in a patterned way, and now all of its parts can be used quickly.

63
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:46,000
You can continue to add various styles to create your own patterned resource library.

64
00:05:46,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Tip 3. In addition to the extra-partition embroidery style mentioned earlier, most of the parts can be cross-styled and automatically create a sewing line.

65
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
You can use your imagination.

66
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Create various interesting fashion combinations.

67
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
See you in the next video. Bye bye.

